{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And everyone whose heart lifted him came</b> — He says this concerning the skilled craftsmen who performed the work, for we do not find the phrase 'lifting of heart' regarding the donors, but rather he uses the term 'willingness' (nedivut) for them. And the meaning of <b>whose heart lifted him</b> is: to draw near to the craft, for there was none among them whom a teacher had taught these crafts, nor anyone who had trained his hands in them at all; rather, he found in his nature that he knew how to do so, and his heart was lifted up in the ways of HaShem (II Chronicles 17:6) to come before Moses to say to him, 'I will do all that my master speaks.' And I have already mentioned this in the other portion (Ramban on Exodus 31:2). Now, he says that before Moses came everyone whose heart lifted him to draw near to the craft, and everyone whose spirit moved him brought the offering; and then Moses said to all of them that HaShem has called by name Betzalel and Oholiav (Exodus 35:30), and afterward Moses called to them — 'and every wise-hearted man' (Exodus 36:2) — that they should come before him, and he gave them the donation."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:38.095980518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}